# Copy to .env and fill in real values. docker compose reads this automatically.

# IANA time zone used to evaluate scheduled-task cron expressions (default UTC).
SCHEDULER_TIMEZONE=UTC

# How hard the backup is allowed to lean on the disk, relative to everything else on the machine:
# Normal (default), Low, or Idle. Covers every read this app makes — the diff, the dedup probe, 7-Zip and
# the uploads — because it is applied to the process before it has a second thread.
#
# Set it if backups make the rest of the box unresponsive: on a NAS also serving SMB, a directory listing
# queueing behind the backup's reads for seconds is what this is for. Low still gets a share of a contended
# disk, just the smallest one; Idle takes disk time only when nobody else wants any, which is the strongest
# yield and can starve a backup outright behind a busy fileserver.
#
# CAVEAT, read before expecting anything: only the BFQ IO scheduler acts on this. Under mq-deadline or none
# — between them the default nearly everywhere — the value is accepted and then never consulted, and the
# setting does nothing at all. Check the scheduler in force first, the one in brackets:
#   cat /sys/block/sda/queue/scheduler
# The startup log says what was requested and whether the kernel took it.
BACKUP_IO_PRIORITY=Normal
